<title>CANADA: Scotiabank cuts prime to 4.75 pct from 5.0.</title>
<headline>Scotiabank cuts prime to 4.75 pct from 5.0.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Nova Scotia said on Friday it cut its prime lending rate to 4.75 percent from 5.00percent, effective Tuesday.</p>
<p>The move follows a Bank of Canada rate cut of 25 basis points to 3.25 percent.</p>
<p>Canada's major banks last changed their prime lending rates on October 29, when they lowered them to 5.00 percent from 5.25 percent.</p>
<p>The prime rate is the rate charged by banks on loans to their best customers.</p>
<p>--Reuters Toronto Bureau 416-941-8100</p>
</text>
